  "details": "An int takes up 8 bytes, and can range from 0-255.  But for most use cases, one would never use this to its fullest, wasting bits.\nHaving a ranged parameter could solve this problem, ease on complexity and allow for more user creativity.\nA simple/lazy was to do this would be allowing the user to select ranges from powers of two, and just bit shifting/masking subsequently.\nA better solution would be to reserve a chunk of bits for this \"dynamic range variables\" as one large number(T).  With X_n being each parameter and M_n being thier max value, T can be calculated by the following: T=X_0+(X_1*M_0)+(X_2*M_0*M_1) ...\nA specific value can then be extracted with X_1 = floor(T/M_2)%M_1\nAlittle more computationally expesive, but favoring space *may* be more important.  Just an idea!  Hope it helps",
